      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the relationship between the least common multiple (LCM) and greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers.\n\nGiven:\n- LCM of two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) can be calculated using the formula: \n\\[ l.c.m = \\frac{|a \\times b|}{\\mathrm{GCD}(a, b)} \\]\n\nIn this problem, we are given the LCM and GCD:\n- LCM \\(l.c.m = 36\\)\n- GCD \\(\\mathrm{GCD}(a, b) = 6\\)\n\nWe also know that GCD and LCM of two numbers are related by:\n\\[ l.c.m \\times \\mathrm{GCD} = |a \\times b| \\]\n\nUsing the LCM and GCD values, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 36 \\times 6 = |a \\times b| \\]\n\\[ 216 = |a \\times b| \\]\n\nSo, we need to find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) such that \\(a \\times b = 216\\) and \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are integers with a GCD of 6. Let's denote \\(a = 6 \\times x\\) and \\(b = 6 \\times y\\) to satisfy the GCD condition:\n\\[ \\mathrm{GCD}(a, b) = 6 = 6 \\times \\frac{x}{6} \\times 6 \\times \\frac{y}{6} \\]\n\nTherefore, we need to find \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) such that:\n\\[ x \\times y = 36 \\]\n\nPossible pairs \\((x, y)\\) that satisfy \\(x \\times y = 36\\) and ensure \\(a \\times b = 216\\) are the factors of 36. The pairs are:\n- \\((1, 36)\\)\n- \\((36, 1)\\)\n- \\((2, 18)\\)\n- \\((18, 2)\\)\n- \\((3, 12)\\)\n- \\((12, 3)\\)\n- \\((4, 9)\\)\n- \\((9, 4)\\)\n- \\((6, 6)\\)\n\nWe can verify which pair satisfies \\(a \\times b = 216\\):\n- \\(a = 72 \\times 1 = 72\\)\n- \\(b = 3 \\times 6 = 18\\)\n- \\(a = 6 \\times 6 = 36\\)\n- \\(b = 6 \\times 3 = 18\\)\n- \\(a = 6 \\times 2 = 12\\)\n- \\(b = 6 \\times 6 = 36\\)\n- \\(a = 6 \\times 1 = 12\\)\n- \\(b = 6 \\times 9 = 54\\)\n\nThus, the pairs that match the conditions are \\((36 \\times 18) = 648\\), \\((36 \\times 12) = 432\\), and \\((648 \\div 36 = 432 \\div 18 = 18 = 648 \\div 12 = 432 \\div 9 = 432 \\div 36 = 1\\)).\n\nFinally, the product \\(a \\times b = 4 \\times 3 = 12\\). To get the correct single answer, the product \\(a \\times b = 216 / 6 = 36 \\times 6 = 216\\).\n\nTherefore, the answer is inserted in \\(\\boxed{216}\\).",
